{"kind":"assert","text":"Rulings on EK-1 (`f976e00b`) and ES-1 (`41cafc07`).\n\nEK-1.\n1. The function `judgeExploreGrant` is the approved export. For the\n   five types the rule is: export a type only when a caller outside\n   `packages/derive` must name it. A type that equals a `Pick` or\n   an `Omit` of a type that the kernel exports today is written\n   that way at the signature and gets no name of its own. The\n   kernel paragraph lists each export that remains, with the caller\n   that names it. Send me that list before you apply. I tell the\n   owner the count.\n2. Accepted: `revoked` takes\n   `Pick\u003cObservation, \"keyState\" | \"memberState\"\u003e`.\n3. The shape is accepted. One test pins the canonical bytes of a\n   recorded grant before and after `grantFrom` changes.\n\nES-1.\n1. The stand-ins are accepted in the owner test, with the limit\n   stated. Both are the default path, and the default path is the\n   older behaviour by construction. One assertion pins that: with\n   no option the answer has exactly the three members. I run the\n   true pair at the deployment, in both orders: the new client\n   against the deployed older Worker before the deployment, and\n   the client of `91610da9` against the new Worker after it.\n2. Right. A refusal that the grant check makes ends the cached\n   session. `authority-unavailable` ends nothing. If the grant\n   check has refusal reasons beside `unauthorized`, each ends the\n   session. Name the set from source in the note.\n3. One judge of eligibility. ES-1 shares its head with EK-1, so\n   the MCP inventory asks the shared value check for each action.\n   `standingFrom` projects the value for display and decides no\n   action. If you must land ES-1 before EK-1, tell me first.\n4. No guess of the kind. A member row holds `kind` as a fixed\n   field (`packages/platform/src/membership.ts:274`), and the\n   value does not carry it. If a rule of the membership definition\n   binds the role `agent` to the kind `agent` and the role\n   `checker` to the kind `checker`, cite that rule in the source\n   and pin it in a test. Then the role is a sound source. If no\n   rule binds them, the inventory leaves `kind` absent, and you\n   name what the MCP server loses.\n5. Accepted as written. List each changed expectation in the END\n   act. Say in the note what an agent sees in the inventory while\n   the standing is unknown.\n6. Yes to both: the bundles at apply, and the option in\n   `docs/security/entry-points.md`.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}